    "id": "F1",
    "path": "sections.story.9",
    "category": "facts",
    "severity": "fix",
    "problem": "正文只写南卡罗来纳代表团“意见分裂”/“was divided”，没有交代原因。读者容易误以为南卡罗来纳有人反对宪法本身。据脚注，平克尼和巴特勒投反对票，是因为不喜欢这个含糊的签署格式。",
    "evidence": [
     {
      "id": "F-E25",
      "quote": "Gen. Pinckney and Mr. Butler disliked the equivocal form of signing, and on that account voted in the negative."
     },
     {
      "id": "F-E22",
      "quote": "South Carolina, divided."
     }
    ],
    "proposed": "中文在句末补：“（据麦迪逊注，平克尼和巴特勒因不喜欢这一含糊的签署格式而投了反对票）”。英文对应补：“(Madison notes that Pinckney and Butler disliked the equivocal form of signing and on that account voted in the negative.)”"
   },
   {
    "id": "F2",
    "path": "sections.story.10",
    "category": "facts",
    "severity": "fix",
    "problem": "麦迪逊明确记下椅背上画的是“a rising sun”。正文中英文都只写“画着的太阳”/“a sun happened to be painted”，省掉了这一记录细节；中文“议长椅背”与同段“主席身后”的称呼也不统一。",
    "evidence": [
     {
      "id": "F-E10",
      "quote": "at the back of which a rising sun happened to be painted"
     }
    ],
    "proposed": "英文改为“at the back of which a rising sun happened to be painted”。中文改为“望着主席椅背上画着的一轮初升的太阳”，并统一用“主席”。"
   }
